-// errors Windows gives such a system (and Miles, for one, runs silent).
+// winmm wave output: one wave output device (device 0, also the wave
+// mapper's) on an SDL audio stream per open handle. Programs that mix
+// themselves (Miles) hand over PCM blocks in WAVEHDRs; a block is done when
+// the stream has consumed its bytes.
+//
+// Callbacks follow Wine's winmm: WOM_OPEN and WOM_CLOSE are delivered from
+// waveOutOpen / waveOutClose on the calling thread, WOM_DONE from the
+// device's own thread (a guest thread here) in the order the blocks were
+// written. waveOutReset returns every queued block (WOM_DONE from the
+// device thread) before it returns. CALLBACK_FUNCTION and CALLBACK_EVENT
+// are implemented; window and thread callbacks, looping blocks, and other
+// open flags are stops that name themselves.
